================================================================================
⚠️ 230V AC MAINS ELECTRICAL SAFETY DISCLAIMER & LIABILITY WAIVER (CRITICAL)
================================================================================
This project contains hardware circuit schematics, PCB layout Gerber files,
firmware code, and wiring instructions designed to interface with 110V – 240V AC
household mains electricity.

1. LETHAL VOLTAGE HAZARD: Mains voltage (110V - 240V AC) can cause fatal electric
   shocks, electrocution, severe burns, electrical arc flashes, and catastrophic
   household fires.
2. EDUCATIONAL PURPOSE ONLY: All schematics, PCBs, firmware, and documentation
   are provided strictly for educational, informational, and experimental research
   purposes.
3. NO LIABILITY / WAIVER: The author(s), creator(s), and contributor(s) accept
   ABSOLUTELY NO LIABILITY OR RESPONSIBILITY for any death, personal injury,
   burns, electrocution, electrical fires, property destruction, hardware damage,
   or municipal/national electrical code violations resulting directly or
   indirectly from the assembly, soldering, fabrication, testing, installation,
   or operation of these designs.
4. AT YOUR OWN RISK: Anyone who fabricates, solders, tests, or connects these
   boards to mains electricity does so ENTIRELY AT THEIR OWN RISK. Always turn
   off the main circuit breaker (MCB) before working on any AC circuit, use
   flame-retardant enclosures, and consult a certified, licensed electrician to
   ensure full compliance with local electrical safety regulations (NEC, IEC, CE).
